#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1065 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "The sister half of the PMDA-SD1065 and PMDA-SD1465 gate(s) (minted 2026-09-11, M16/T1-35+T1-36 -- ONE sister for both board rows, R-5.26). The RDOMAIN column is absent (None satisfied) while row 1 populates IDVAR and row 2 populates IDVARVAL, so the union trigger holds on both rows; Sensitivity is Dataset, so the absence is reported ONCE. Same dataset shape as the parents' skipped_no_rdomain_column scenarios: the parents skip, this rule reports."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset CO class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Comments"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col COVAL    type=Char label="Comment"
---
S1 |     | 1 | AESEQ |   | Comment on the AE record
S1 | 001 | 2 |       | 3 | Comment keyed by value only
